@startuml Player Recruitment Sequence Diagram
actor "Team Owner" as Owner
participant "Frontend Client" as Client
participant "Express API Server" as API
database "MySQL Database" as DB
actor "Invited Player" as Player
== Send Recruitment Request ==
Owner -> Client: Selects player and clicks "Recruit"
Client -> API: POST /api/recruitment {teamId, playerProfileId}
API -> DB: Query Team and PlayerProfile
DB --> API: Returns details
API -> API: Check ownership (isOwner?)
alt isOwner == true
  API -> DB: Create RecruitmentRequest (status: PENDING)
  DB --> API: Return Request created
  API --> Client: 201 Created (Request info)
  Client --> Owner: Show "Invitation Sent Successfully"
else isOwner == false
  API --> Client: 403 Forbidden
  Client --> Owner: Show Error
end
== View & Respond to Request ==
Player -> Client: Opens Notifications
Client -> API: GET /api/recruitment/incoming
API -> DB: Query RecruitmentRequests for Player
DB --> API: Return List
Client --> Player: Render Incoming Invitations
Player -> Client: Clicks "Accept Invitation"
Client -> API: POST /api/recruitment/:id/respond {status: "ACCEPTED"}
API -> DB: Query and verify Request details
DB --> API: Return Request
API -> API: Verify request belongs to Player
API -> DB: Update Request status to ACCEPTED
API -> DB: Create TeamMember record (teamId, playerProfileId)
DB --> API: Return Success
API --> Client: 200 OK (Updated Request)
Client --> Player: Show "Joined Team successfully"
@enduml
